    "details": "<p><strong>Event Details</strong></p>\n<ul dir=\"ltr\">\n<li><strong>Date:</strong> 23 October 2026</li>\n<li><strong>Time:</strong> 10:30 AM &ndash; 12:00 PM</li>\n<li><strong>Venue:</strong> LAB 1, 2, 3, 4, I.T.S. Engineering College, Greater Noida</li>\n<li><strong>Registration Fee:</strong> ₹300 per team</li>\n<li><strong>Prize Pool:</strong> ₹15,000</li>\n<li><strong>Team Size:</strong> ️ 5 participants/team</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Valorant &ndash; Battle Zone is a competitive esports event at TechTrix'26, bringing teams together for an intense multiplayer tournament. Participants compete across tournament rounds, demonstrating teamwork, communication, coordination, strategic decision-making, and consistency. This is a BYOD (Bring Your Own Device) event &mdash; high-speed Wi-Fi and snacks will be provided, but participants must bring their own laptops/devices.</p>\n<p><strong>Guidelines</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Team Size</strong></p>\n<ul dir=\"ltr\">\n<li>5 participants per team</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Requirements</strong></p>\n<ul dir=\"ltr\">\n<li>Participants must bring their own laptops/devices required for the game</li>\n<li>Only registered players are permitted to participate</li>\n<li>Participants must report before their scheduled match</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Tournament Rules</strong></p>\n<ul dir=\"ltr\">\n<li>The tournament format (league, knockout, or hybrid) will be finalized by the organizers based on the number of registrations</li>\n<li>Maps, servers, and match settings will be fixed by the organizers</li>\n<li>The organizer's recorded result will be treated as the official result</li>\n<li>Genuine technical problems must be reported immediately to the referee/coordinator; a technical issue caused by a participant's own unauthorized software or settings will normally be treated as the participant's responsibility</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Judging Criteria</strong></p>\n<p>The winner is determined according to the final tournament format and match results declared by the organizers &mdash; based on match wins/progression through the league, knockout, or hybrid bracket as configured.</p>\n<p><strong>Disqualification</strong></p>\n<p>The following are strictly prohibited and may result in disqualification:</p>\n<ul dir=\"ltr\">\n<li>Account sharing</li>\n<li>Cheat software, hacks, macros, or unauthorized scripts</li>\n<li>Exploiting known game bugs or glitches</li>\n<li>Deliberate disconnections or match manipulation</li>\n<li>Interference with another player's system or event infrastructure</li>\n</ul>\n<p>The Event Jury/Referee/Technical Committee holds final authority on match outcomes, penalties, and rule interpretation.</p>\n<p><strong data-start=\"2611\" data-end=\"2637\">NOTE: Registration Fees are not refundable.</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Opportunities for Winners:</strong></p>\n<p>Get <strong>Truscholar Certificate and credits</strong> -- Up to <strong>₹14.2+ Lakhs</strong></p>",
